# Include Directory

Project headers in this directory are used as module contracts for the firmware.
Most implementations still live in `src/main.cpp`; the headers keep ownership,
threading, and safety notes close to the APIs they describe.

## Main Module Groups

| Area | Headers |
|---|---|
| Control protocols | `control_protocol.h`, `crsf_receiver.h`, `crsf_control.h`, `ibus_receiver.h`, `ibus_control.h`, `nrf_telemetry.h` |
| Motors and filtering | `motor_module.h`, `RpmNotchFilter.h`, `motor_fft_test.h`, `BiquadFilter.h`, `DynamicNotchFilter.h` |
| Sensors | `imu_module.h`, `tof_module.h`, `tof_altitude.h`, `baro_module.h`, `gps_module.h`, `battery_module.h`, `sensor_calibration.h`, `mag_calibration.h` |
| PID and tuning | `fcu_pid.h`, `pid_block.h`, `pid_webserver.h`, `gain_schedule.h` |
| Autonomy/GNC | `frames.h`, `math3.h`, `ekf_estimator.h`, `estimator_health.h`, `cascaded_controller.h`, `velocity_controller.h`, `position_controller.h`, `return_to_home.h`, `landing_controller.h`, `auto_takeoff.h`, `flight_modes.h`, `flight_state_machine.h`, `sim_harness.h` |
| Support | `autonomy_uart.h`, `camera_gimbal.h`, `fcu_nvs.h`, `led_blinker.h` |

## Conventions

- Headers should document which task writes shared state and which locks guard
  it. Use the existing module banners as the local style.
- Prefer small POD snapshot structs for cross-task data. Avoid heap ownership
  in flight-loop paths.
- Keep build-flag defaults in `src/main.cpp` and `platformio.ini`; headers
  should describe the contract, not silently change feature gates.
- Safety-sensitive comments should name exact failure behavior: motor stop,
  failsafe latch, telemetry-only, or log-only.

## Current Control Flow

`crsfControlTask` or a legacy input task writes a `ControlPacket`. The 500 Hz
`flightTask` reads that packet, polls IMU, updates filters/PID, and writes four
DShot outputs. `sensorTask` refreshes slower sensors and battery state.

Experimental EKF/autonomy headers are compiled in, but direct mixer authority is
still gated by `ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_EKF_CONTROL`.
